      },
      "lineNbr": 31,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000381
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-12-05T00:29:52Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think you should have a different command to \"add\" an attachment, instead of embedding creation in the activate logic. The reason is that there\u0027s a remove command, which makes it natural to expect an add one.\n\nIf you want to reduce the number of commands, the activate one can be modified to take an input boolean parameters to signal whether the line should be enabled or not. E.g. attachment-enable  -d (where  -d means disable).\n\nFinally, I think \"enable/disable\" is a better wording, as activate has generally meaning of \"To put into action, to put to work\", which doesn\u0027t make much sense in this context.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 31,
        "startChar": 13,
        "endLine": 31,
        "endChar": 31
      },
      "revId": "d413abd2e5ada965d706a166c69d8b11c56bd26f",
      "serverId": "2a2bfe1b-c5c2-48ed-9ac8-16438ab24388",
      "unresolved": false
    },
